WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.941
Free wins first, trades second.

2
00:00:02.221 --> 00:00:07.491
Anthropic’s cost guidance sorts every cost lever into two groups, and the order matters.

3
00:00:07.771 --> 00:00:16.133
Free wins lower what you pay without lowering output quality: prompt caching (usually the largest), trimming input, and batch processing.

4
00:00:16.413 --> 00:00:24.093
Tradeoffs exchange capability for cost: effort, model choice, and multi-model designs such as routers and cascades.

5
00:00:24.373 --> 00:00:27.360
Do the free wins first and leave caching on permanently.

6
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:33.933
Pull the trades last, one at a time, against an eval, because each one can quietly cost you answers.

7
00:00:34.213 --> 00:00:36.112
This lesson follows that order.

8
00:00:36.392 --> 00:00:50.088
It spends the most time on caching, because caching is where most teams lose money without noticing, and it ends with routing, because routing is where most teams spend engineering effort before measuring whether a simpler option would do.
